# Refuse dpkg runs when overlayroot is not active (design section 6.3).
# With the read-only-root + overlay architecture an apt/dpkg session on a
# fallback rw root writes the lower layer directly and silently breaks the
# "OTA replaces the whole system" consistency premise. The check is a
# no-op whenever / is the expected overlay.
DPkg::Pre-Invoke { "findmnt -n -o FSTYPE / | grep -q overlay || { echo 'ERROR: overlayroot not active, refusing dpkg (reboot or fix /etc/overlayroot.conf)'; exit 1; }"; };
